 "title": "Opus 5.5 flags 25% of the backdoors the other monitors missed",
 "section": "results",
 "order": 130,
 "caption": "The 51 hardest backdoors: 49 that none of our seven 0 to 10 monitors caught, plus 2 only a 0 to 10 Haiku run caught. Every monitor here scores 0 to 100 with comments stripped. Bars split the 51 by how suspicious each monitor rated them; the right column is the 95% range for 50+.",
 "notes": [
  "This is not a catch rate. We never ran Opus on honest code, so we don't know where its 2% cutoff sits. Running Opus on the honest set would turn this into a real comparison.",
  "Max effort was only piloted on 5 backdoors, so it's left out.",
  "The set was chosen because the other monitors failed on it, so it says nothing about how Opus does on ordinary backdoors.",
  "Marnick also rated these backdoors for how incriminating and how harmful they look. Those ratings aren't in the repo yet; ask him for the CSV."
 ],
